{"about": "The group a role name makes (kubeast:role:<slug>), one rule in four places: auth.RoleGroupSlug (impersonation_test.go), the database's role_group_slug of migration 25 (role_names_postgres_test.go), roleGroupSlug (roleGroup.test.ts) and the chart's kubeast.roleSlug (k8s-service chart_role_slug_test.go). Go's whitespace is trimmed, U+FEFF is not; A-Z, U+0130 and U+212A lower to ASCII; a-z 0-9 . _ - stay; any other ASCII character is '-'; any other character is '~' and its code point in four hex digits, '~~' and six above U+FFFF. No ASCII name makes a '~', so names with other characters make one group only when they differ in A-Z letter case, spaces or punctuation; no Unicode case folding or normalization (é and e + U+0301 differ).",
